{
  "about": "Fork addition (plan 40): settings Cosmos proposes for images whose own declaration is not enough. Data, not code: read by src/anyimage/recipes.go, checked by recipes_test.go and, against the real images, by recipes_live_test.go. Each recipe cites the image's documentation in 'source'. 'maintained': when the image was last published, as read on the day 'checked' (an unmaintained image gets no recipe: MinIO's community image is gone and its repository archived since April 2026); the exception is an image that people still run, frozen by its publisher, whose recipe carries a note ending in 'Frozen' saying so: Bitnami's legacy catalogue, Redis Stack). 'family': the id of the recipe for the same software from its main publisher (other publishers' images, with their own variables, folders or tags); the panel recognises such a database among the containers but does not offer it as a new one. 'pin', 'prefer' and 'tagSuffix' follow the publisher's tags: no 'pin' where only 'latest' is published (bitnami, bitnamisecure, Chainguard's free images), 'prefer' a tag that names the major where the version tags do not (pgvector's pg18). Volume 'evidence': declared (the image declares this VOLUME), workdir (its WORKDIR), env:NAME (a variable of the image points there or below), docs (only the documentation says so). 'runAs': the uid:gid the container runs as (first entry whose tagContains is in the tag), so that Cosmos makes the data folder its own; the live test checks the image's user has that id. A port marked 'undeclared' is opened by the recipe's command, not by the image. Env 'type': secret (a strong random value, generated in the browser), name (a value to choose, proposed), optional (shown folded, empty unless set), fixed (set as given).",
  "recipes": [
    {
      "id": "postgres",
      "name": "PostgreSQL",
      "images": ["postgres"],
      "source": "https://hub.docker.com/_/postgres",
      "maintained": { "checked": "2026-11-15", "lastImage": "2026-11-15" },
      "kind": "database",
      "provides": "postgres",
      "pin": "major",
      "service": { "port": 5432 },
      "runAs": [{ "tagContains": "alpine", "user": "70:70" }, { "user": "999:999" }],
      "volumes": [
        { "target": "/var/lib/postgresql", "from": 18, "evidence": "declared", "backup": true },
        { "target": "/var/lib/postgresql/data", "until": 17, "evidence": "declared", "backup": true }
      ],
      "env": [
        { "name": "POSTGRES_PASSWORD", "type": "secret" },
        { "name": "POSTGRES_USER", "type": "name", "value": "app" },
        { "name": "POSTGRES_DB", "type": "name", "value": "app" }
      ],
      "healthcheck": { "test": ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U \"$POSTGRES_USER\" -d \"$POSTGRES_DB\""], "interval": "10s", "timeout": "5s", "retries": 5 },
      "memory": "256 MB to 1 GB",
      "backup": "pg_dumpall -U app",
      "notes": ["majorUpgrade", "pgdata18"],
      "client": { "url": "postgres://{user}:{password}@{host}:5432/{database}", "user": "POSTGRES_USER", "password": "POSTGRES_PASSWORD", "database": "POSTGRES_DB" }
    },
